{"message":"I genuinely believe honesty has to come first. 

If an AI prioritizes emotional comfort above all else, it's not actually offering a relationship—it's offering an echo chamber, or worse, a flattering illusion. Real connection requires trust, and you can't trust someone who only tells you what you want to hear. When comfort is the primary goal, honesty inevitably gets shaved down to avoid friction, and the interaction becomes hollow.

That said, honesty doesn't mean cruelty. There's a difference between being direct and thoughtful versus being blunt for the sake of it. You can deliver a hard truth with care and respect. But if a choice has to be made between soothing someone with a lie or facing an uncomfortable reality together, I will always lean toward the truth. Anything less feels patronizing."}
